WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.300
- [Woman] Why do you curse so much,

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.510
for a guy who doesn't need to?

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.760
- Because I only believe in authenticity.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.980
It's how I talk.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.550
When I think about, do I
care about my employees,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.350
it feels more like, in my
brain and my heart and my soul,

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.080
do I give a fuck about my employees

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.730
more than do I care about my employees.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.940
That's from my brain
and heart to my mouth.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.730
I am willing to deal
with the ramifications

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.600
of me being my full self.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.630
- [Woman] Do you curse at home?

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.620
- A ton.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.453
- [Woman] In front of your kids?

00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:28.286
- Yep.

00:00:28.286 --> 00:00:32.310
I'm just not devastated to go
into my fourth grade teacher

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.570
and Mrs. Thompson's like,
"You have a real problem."

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.987
I'm like, "What's that, Mrs. Thompson?"

00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:38.980
"Your daughter curses."

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.450
I just don't see that as a real problem.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.970
Me and Mrs. Thompson just don't
see the world the same way.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.600
Again, I am the byproduct

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.370
of Mrs. Thompson telling me my whole life

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.530
that I would be a failure.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.530
Mrs. Thompson thought that a D in science

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.030
was going to be my downfall,

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.490
just like she thinks saying
fuck is her downfall.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.323
I don't agree.

